{"id":"lsvmbus.8","n":"lsvmbus","s":"8","src":{"u":{"pkg":"linux-cloud-tools-common","ver":"5.15.0-204.214","repo":"jammy-updates/main","url":"http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/l/linux/linux-cloud-tools-common_5.15.0-204.214_all.deb","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/lsvmbus.8.gz","sha256":"71e7a51465959cce295955acfca10ccea3adf9a1f1199def83bf7a6e3092c526","date":"","origin":"","also":["linux-intel-iotg-cloud-tools-common"]}},"nopt":{"u":1},"desc":"List Hyper-V VMBus devices","u":[["NAME","<p>lsvmbus - List Hyper-V VMBus devices</p>"],["SYNOPSIS","<p><b>lsvmbus [-vv]</b></p>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p><b>lsvmbus</b> displays devices attached to the Hyper-V VMBus.</p>"],["OPTIONS","<dl><dt data-o=\"\"><b>-v</b></dt><dd>With -v more information is printed including the VMBus Rel_ID, class ID, Rel_ID, and which channel is bound to which virtual processor. Use -vv for additional detail including the Device_ID and the sysfs path.</dd></dl>"],["AUTHORS","<pre>Written by Dexuan Cui &lt;decui@microsoft.com&gt;</pre>"]]}